    "done_when": "A probe script, kept under the run directory, loads the project page for nova, reckon and imas-ambix in headless Chromium through an SSH tunnel to 98dci4-srv-1006 port 8765 (ssh -N -L <local port>:localhost:8765 98dci4-srv-1006), cold and again warm, and measures for each load: the time until the plan list shows non-zero progress bars; the time until the graph, velocity (project and all scopes) and crew views are populated; the bytes the home view transfers; the bytes and the time until the first screen of the figure list shows its thumbnails (nova and power_convertor); and the console errors. Ten plans per project are drawn at random and the bar each surface shows is compared with the section's progress function. The gate is hard: progress bars within 2 s warm; every view populated within 3 s warm and 10 s cold; no console error; the home view under 500 KB; the first screen of nova's and power_convertor's figure lists under 2 MB with every thumbnail shown within 2 s warm; all thirty sampled plans agreeing on every surface. A failed gate names the section that owns the miss. The negative control runs the same probe against a temporary reckon serve on another port on the fleet allocation, started from a git worktree at the plan's base revision (the commit before the plan's first section merged), and the gate must fail there. Record the report, with the host, the load average and the UTC window of each pass, in docs/evidence/archive/the-site-answers-fast-and-agrees-landed.html under an s11 anchor: that file is cumulative, so splice your section in and remove nothing (git diff HEAD on it must show no removed line), and draw any timing chart under docs/figures/the-site-answers-fast-and-agrees/the-site-is-measured. Do not run browsers or servers on a login node; the probe runs on the fleet allocation. Every log sits under the run directory and ends in EXIT=. If the tunnel cannot be opened from the worker's environment, stop blocked and say so rather than measuring something else.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
